Original commit body from 58443d33434a41e48c8f4f174d0d5a38a17535a2:

Dependabot alerts on every pinned version in any manifest on the default
branch, fixture or not. The aardvark-dns fixture's Cargo.lock drew five
alerts for a crate the repo never builds; #1778 removed it. This guard
keeps the next fixture from doing the same: a tracked file fails if its
name is a lockfile (Cargo.lock, package-lock.json, go.sum, uv.lock, ...)
or if it is a requirements*.txt with an exact == pin, unless listed in
ALLOWED with a reason (empty today).

Checked red: with the deleted Cargo.lock restored, the live test fails
and names its path; green on the current tree. Unit cases cover a
lockfile anywhere, exact-pin vs range vs comment in requirements files,
and declaring manifests (pyproject, go.mod, Cargo.toml) staying out of
scope. Version pins inside go.mod / pom.xml / Gemfile are not covered,
as the module docstring states; no fixture of those kinds pins today.

